<title>UK: UK grain traders bid for free market wheat, barley.</title>
<headline>UK grain traders bid for free market wheat, barley.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>UK grain traders bid for licences to export free market wheat and barley at the weekly European Union (EU) tender held on Thursday, the UK Intervention Board for Agricultural Produce said. The board was unable to give further details because there were fewer than three bids, it said.</p>
<p>All bids will be considered at Thursday's weekly EU cereals management committee meeting.</p>
<p>--Christopher Lyddon, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7928</p>
